{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788202034,"nonce":"cJUgX/rxKuDKLSGWX1c1IKN1wsU=","message":"VERIFICATION (backlog verification pass, git-bug 2f2796e, run fbb2c59)\n\nCORRECTED — the CORE PREMISE stands (no verb can use a targetable item on a\ntarget) but FOUR of the five motivating examples are wrong about the mechanism,\nthe stated precondition does not exist in the game, and two acceptance bullets\nare unsatisfiable as a result. There is also a force-pause modal on the exact\nmethod the verb must call, and a private-field problem that makes the naive\nimplementation a silent no-op.\n\n=====================================================================\nCONFIRMED FIRST\n=====================================================================\n\n- \"The verb surface has exactly one item-use verb, `consume`, and it is INGEST.\"\n  CONFIRMED. `Source/AutoRimmer/PawnOrderVerbs.Consume` is\n  `var job = JobMaker.MakeJob(JobDefOf.Ingest, thing);` and its own header cites\n  `RimWorld/FloatMenuOptionProvider_Ingest`. An unpiped enumeration of `[Verb(`\n  over `Source/AutoRimmer/` finds no other item-use verb.\n- \"That is a THIRD order shape the mod does not model.\" CONFIRMED, and totally:\n  greps for `CompUsable`, `CompTargetable`, `CompUseEffect`, `ITargetingSource`,\n  `Find.Targeter`, `ResurrectionUtility` over `Source/AutoRimmer/` return ZERO\n  hits. No route, dev or player.\n- `RimWorld/CompUsable`, `CompTargetable`, `CompTargetable_SingleCorpse`,\n  `CompTargetable_SinglePawn` all exist (plus `_SingleAnimal`,\n  `_AllPawnsOnTheMap`, `_AllAnimalsOnTheMap`). CONFIRMED.\n- `MechSerumResurrector` and Anomaly's `GhoulResurrectionSerum` both carry\n  `CompProperties_Targetable` with `compClass CompTargetable_SingleCorpse`.\n  CONFIRMED — these two are genuine instances of the shape the issue describes.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 1 — FOUR OF THE FIVE MOTIVATING EXAMPLES ARE NOT THIS SHAPE\n=====================================================================\n\n* **`MechSerumHealer` — not targetable, and ALREADY REACHABLE TODAY.** Its def\n  (`ThingDefs_Items/Items_Exotic.xml`) has no `CompProperties_Targetable` at all;\n  it has `CompProperties_UseEffect` with `compClass CompUseEffect_FixWorstHealthCondition`\n  and the user heals ITSELF. And the same file defines\n  `RecipeDef AdministerMechSerumHealer` with\n  `\u003cworkerClass\u003eRecipe_AdministerUsableItem\u003c/workerClass\u003e`, listed on\n  `Races_Humanlike.xml`. `Source/AutoRimmer/MedicalBillVerbs.ScanSurgeries`\n  enumerates `pawn.def.AllRecipes` and calls `recipe.Worker.AvailableReport(pawn)`,\n  so **`surgery-options` / `surgery-add` already surface healer-serum\n  administration.** One of the five items is not missing.\n\n* **Psychic shock lance and insanity lance — apparel with a VERB, not comps.**\n  `ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Utility.xml`: `Apparel_PsychicShockLance` /\n  `Apparel_PsychicInsanityLance` carry `verbClass Verb_CastTargetEffectLances`,\n  `hasStandardCommand true`, `onlyManualCast True`. They are cast from a\n  `Command_VerbTarget` gizmo, not a float menu. **They ARE unreachable, for a\n  different reason**: `RimWorld/FloatMenuUtility.GetRangedAttackAction` — which\n  `PawnOrderVerbs.Attack` reproduces — reads\n  `Verb primaryVerb = pawn.equipment.PrimaryEq.PrimaryVerb;` and nothing else,\n  and `Verse/Pawn.TryGetAttackVerb` only reaches apparel under\n  `allowManualCastWeapons`, which `GetRangedAttackAction` never passes. So this\n  is a FOURTH order shape (equipped-apparel manual-cast verb) and **building the\n  `use` verb this issue specifies will not deliver it.** It deserves its own\n  issue or its own scope line.\n\n* **EMP grenade, smokepop belt, firefoam popper — none of the three.**\n  `Weapon_GrenadeEMP` is a WEAPON (`RangedIndustrialGrenades.xml`);\n  `Apparel_SmokepopBelt` is APPAREL that auto-triggers (`Apparel_Packs.xml`);\n  `FirefoamPopper` is a BUILDING (`Buildings_Misc.xml`). None has\n  `CompProperties_Usable`. The \"thrown at a position\" framing is wrong for all\n  three.\n\nNet: of the five items named as motivation, TWO are the described shape\n(resurrector serums), ONE is already reachable (healer serum), and TWO belong to\nother shapes entirely. The issue is still worth doing — the resurrector case\nalone justifies it — but its scope paragraph should be rewritten before dispatch\nor the worker will chase lances.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 2 — \"THE PAWN MUST BE CARRYING THE ITEM\" IS NOT A GAME RULE, AND TWO\nACCEPTANCE BULLETS DEPEND ON IT\n=====================================================================\n\n`RimWorld/CompUsable.CanBeUsedBy` gates on reachability and reservation, not\npossession:\n\n    if (!ignoreReserveAndReachable \u0026\u0026 !p.CanReach(parent, PathEndMode.Touch, Danger.Deadly))\n    {\n        return \"NoPath\".Translate();\n    }\n\nand `RimWorld/JobDriver_UseItem.MakeNewToils` opens with\n`yield return Toils_Goto.GotoThing(TargetIndex.A, ...)` — the pawn WALKS TO the\nitem. For the resurrector specifically, `RimWorld/JobDriver_Resurrect.MakeNewToils`\npicks it up as part of the job: `yield return Toils_Haul.StartCarryThing(TargetIndex.B);`.\n\nConsequences for the acceptance:\n- Bullet 1 (\"use a CARRIED targetable item\") mandates a gate the game does not\n  have — a verb enforcing it would fabricate a restriction, which is the exact\n  failure the `auto_arm` decision-log entry warns about.\n- Bullet 3 (\"the pawn not carrying the item is its own named refusal\") is\n  **untestable, because the condition cannot arise.** The genuine distinct\n  refusals are `\"NoPath\"` and the reservation reasons from `CanBeUsedBy`.\n- Bullet 5 (\"a read that lists what a CARRIED item may be used on\") inherits the\n  same error; drop the word.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 3 — THE \"TWO DIFFERENT MENUS\" REASONING IS WRONG (THE CONCLUSION IS\nRIGHT)\n=====================================================================\n\n`orders` surfaces none of this — CONFIRMED, `PawnOrderVerbs.Orders` delegates to\n`ScanWorkGivers`, which walks `WorkGiverDef`s and never touches\n`Thing.GetFloatMenuOptions`. But they are not different MENUS. Both\n`FloatMenuOptionProvider_FromThing` and `FloatMenuOptionProvider_WorkGivers` are\n`FloatMenuOptionProvider` subclasses driven by the same `FloatMenuMakerMap` pass,\nand `FloatMenuOptionProvider_FromThing.GetOptionsFor` is\n`foreach (FloatMenuOption floatMenuOption in clickedThing.GetFloatMenuOptions(context.FirstSelectedPawn))`\n-\u003e `Verse/ThingWithComps.GetFloatMenuOptions` -\u003e `comps[i].CompFloatMenuOptions(selPawn)`.\nThe boundary the issue wants stated explicitly is **provider**, not menu, and the\noperative difference is that the player right-clicks the SERUM, not the corpse.\nThat is a better sentence for the code comment than the one in the body.\n\n=====================================================================\nTHREE THINGS THE ISSUE MISSES, AND THE FIRST TWO ARE BLOCKING\n=====================================================================\n\n**MISS 1 — `new Dialog_MessageBox` IS ON THE EXECUTION PATH OF THE EXACT METHOD\nA `use` VERB MUST CALL.** `RimWorld/CompUsable.TryStartUseJob`:\n\n    if (text.NullOrEmpty()) { StartJob(); }\n    else { Find.WindowStack.Add(Dialog_MessageBox.CreateConfirmation(text, StartJob)); }\n\n`text` is the concatenation of every `CompUseEffect.ConfirmMessage(pawn)`;\noverriders in 1.6 are `CompUseEffect_CallBossgroup`,\n`CompUseEffect_InstallImplantMechlink` and `CompUseEffect_GainAbility`.\n`Dialog_MessageBox` sets `forcePause = true`, so per 1.7/1.8 this halts every\nsubsequent `advance` at 0 ticks until 3.5 ships. This is the SECOND shape from\nDESIGN's 2026-08-31 amendment — a modal on a utility's own execution path, not\nbehind an option delegate — and it is the dangerous one. The verb must pre-check\nthe `ConfirmMessage` set and re-derive it as a result field, or reproduce\n`StartJob` without the wrapper.\n\n**MISS 2 — SETTING `targetB` ON THE JOB DOES NOT SET THE EFFECT'S TARGET. THE\nNAIVE IMPLEMENTATION RUNS TO COMPLETION AND RESURRECTS NOBODY.**\n`RimWorld/CompTargetable` keeps `private Thing selectedTarget;` and `private Pawn caster;`,\nand `CompTargetable.DoEffect` reads the FIELD, not the job:\n\n    if ((PlayerChoosesTarget \u0026\u0026 selectedTarget == null) || (selectedTarget != null \u0026\u0026 !GetTargetingParameters().CanTarget(selectedTarget)))\n    {\n        return;\n    }\n\n`PlayerChoosesTarget =\u003e true` on both `_SingleCorpse` and `_SinglePawn`. The job's\n`targetB` is used only for reservation, fail-conditions and mote attachment\n(`JobDriver_UseItem.TryMakePreToilReservations` / `PrepareToUse`). So\n`JobMaker.MakeJob(useJob, item, corpse)` + `TryTakeOrderedJob` succeeds, the pawn\nwalks over, the job completes, and the effect silently does nothing. **That is a\nfalse positive of exactly the class `4087644` is about**, and it would be\ndiscovered at acceptance rather than at design time.\n\nThe only public setter is `CompTargetable.OrderForceTarget(LocalTargetInfo)` —\nand it is not usable cold, because it reads `caster`, which is set only by\n`SelectedUseOption` (which itself calls `Find.Targeter.BeginTargeting`). With\n`caster == null` it reaches `CanBeUsedBy(null)` -\u003e `p.RaceProps` -\u003e NRE, i.e. a\nred error. So the verb needs either reflection to seat both private fields, or a\nre-implementation of `StartJob` plus a write of `selectedTarget`. Either way it\nis a `*Safe`-style guarded route, and the spec should say so.\n\nAlso worth knowing: `CompTargetable.PostExposeData` does\n`Scribe_References.Look(ref selectedTarget, \"selectedTarget\");` — writing that\nfield is a write to SAVE state, not a transient.\n\n**MISS 3 — THERE ARE THREE VALIDATORS, NOT ONE.** The acceptance says \"the gate\nis the comp's own validator\", singular. They are: the USER gate\n`CompUsable.CanBeUsedBy` (flesh, mutant whitelist, planet layer, power, reach,\nreserve, `userMustHaveHediff`, then every `CompUseEffect.CanBeUsedBy`); the\nTARGET gate `CompTargetable.ValidateTarget` plus each subclass override; and\n`GetTargetingParameters().CanTarget(...)`, which `DoEffect` re-checks\nINDEPENDENTLY at execution time (see Miss 2). Reproducing one and not the others\ngives an \"accepted\" that still no-ops.\n\nSmaller, for completeness:\n- `CompUsable.CompFloatMenuOptions` never OMITS the option — it disables it and\n  appends the reason (`floatMenuOption.Label = floatMenuOption.Label + \" (\" + acceptanceReport.Reason + \")\"`).\n  So the reasons the acceptance wants are already strings the game authors; good\n  news, and it means \"the game's own reason\" is satisfiable here (unlike on 3.6).\n- Provider-level gates not named: `FloatMenuOptionProvider.CanTargetDespawned =\u003e false`\n  (a serum inside a container or an inventory offers nothing) and `IgnoreFogged =\u003e true`;\n  `FloatMenuOptionProvider_FromThing` sets `Drafted`, `Undrafted`, `Multiselect`\n  and `CanSelfTarget` all true.\n- Resurrection is a TWO-JOB CHAIN with a 600-tick wait, gated on the user being a\n  player colonist: `CompTargetEffect_Resurrect.DoEffectOn` is\n  `if (user.IsColonistPlayerControlled) { Job job = JobMaker.MakeJob(JobDefOf.Resurrect, target, parent); ... }`\n  — a slave, ghoul or mech user does nothing at all, silently. And\n  `ResurrectionUtility.TryResurrectWithSideEffects` burns the shared Rand twice\n  (`Rand.Chance(DementiaChancePerRotDaysCurve...)`, `BlindnessChance...`) and\n  `TryResurrect` calls `Find.Selector.Select(pawn, ...)` — UI state, on the action\n  path. Legal on an action verb, and the READ this issue also asks for must go\n  nowhere near it.\n- There is no `JobDefOf.UseItem` field. The job is XML-driven off\n  `CompProperties_Usable.useJob`; the serum defs carry `\u003cuseJob\u003eUseItem\u003c/useJob\u003e`\n  and `RimWorld/JobDriver_UseItem` is the driver. `targetA` = the item,\n  `targetB` = the extra target.\n\n=====================================================================\nACCEPTANCE — SUMMARY\n=====================================================================\n\nBullet 1: mis-specified (\"carried\"). Bullet 2: ambiguous (one validator named,\nthree exist). Bullet 3: UNTESTABLE — the condition cannot arise. Bullet 4\n(resurrection leaves `ResurrectionSickness`): needs the bench AND is conditionally\nfalse — `TryResurrectWithSideEffects` applies it only inside\n`if (!pawn.health.WouldDieAfterAddingHediff(hediff))`, so a frail corpse comes\nback clean and a correct implementation fails the test; and\n`GhoulResurrectionSerum` sets `\u003cwithSideEffects\u003efalse\u003c/withSideEffects\u003e` with\n`\u003caddsHediff\u003eResurrectionComa\u003c/addsHediff\u003e`, a different hediff entirely. Bullet 5:\nfine once \"carried\" is dropped.\n\nRecommended addition to the acceptance, since Miss 2 is the failure this issue\nwould otherwise ship: **assert that the corpse is gone and a living pawn exists\nafterward** — not merely that the job was accepted. A verb that reports success\non a no-op is the exact defect `4087644` names.\n\n=====================================================================\nWHAT I AM INFERRING, NOT CONFIRMING\n=====================================================================\n\n- That reflection is REQUIRED to seat `caster`/`selectedTarget`. I read that both\n  are private and that the only public setter needs `caster` pre-set; I did not\n  prove there is no third route.\n- That the `ConfirmMessage` set is empty for the two resurrector serums\n  specifically. The three overriders I found are unrelated comps, so it very\n  likely is — but the verb should still pre-check rather than assume.","files":null}]}